  "segment": 1,
  "thesis": "Explanation is selective compression; its purpose, scale, conditions and discarded detail determine usefulness. Feeling understanding differs from articulating testable mechanisms; cheap eloquence increases the need for discriminating commitments. Sincere introspection and generated reasoning are outputs whose causal faithfulness needs independent traces. Motivated reasoning can immunize decisions; audit personal benefits symmetrically without treating motives as refutations. Explanations remain powerful through intervention and exposure to failure; scientific virtues differ and auxiliary assumptions complicate falsification.",
